# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data and weights â€” never committed.
#
# data/       credit-risk datasets under varying and sometimes restrictive
#             licences; several are not ours to redistribute.
# checkpoints/ pretrained weights, hundreds of MB each, regenerable from
#             the pretraining scripts.
#
# The .gitkeep exceptions preserve the template's folder structure so a
# fresh clone still has somewhere to put things.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/raw/
data/raw/*
!data/raw/.gitkeep
!data/processed/
data/processed/*
!data/processed/.gitkeep

checkpoints/*
!checkpoints/.gitkeep

# Generated synthetic datasets. Huge (4.0 GB per LGD variant, 5.4 GB per PD variant)
# and always reproducible from a seed, so never committed. The glob also catches
# `prior_cache_bak/` and friends â€” a bare `prior_cache/` did not, and a set of stray
# backup manifests ended up in commit 82919b1 as a result.
prior_cache*/
*.npz
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors

# Processed datasets. Regenerable from data/raw via python -m src.data.preprocess, and on
# the cluster they live on project storage rather than here.
data/processed/**/*.npy
data/processed/**/*.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results.
#
# results/<task>/<pipeline>/ holds the OFFICIAL outputs and small summaries ARE
# committed â€” they are the record of what was run, and a few hundred KB of CSV is
# worth having in git history. Large arrays go to project storage instead.
#
# logs/ is purely informational and never holds results, so it is fully ignored.
# res/ is the old scratch output dir, kept ignored for local runs.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# res/ â€” local scratch output (checkpoints, figures from the notebooks). The comment
# above claimed this was ignored but no pattern actually matched it, so notebook
# figures showed up as untracked files. Regenerate rather than commit.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
pip-wheel-metadata/

# Virtual environments (local and VSC per-architecture)
.venv/
venv/
venv-*/
env/
ENV/
# The project venv. `.CreditICL/` is the name we use: dotted, so it is hidden and
# sorts with the other tool directories. `CreditICL/` (undotted) is kept ignored too
# so the older layout can never be committed by accident during the switch.
.CreditICL/
CreditICL/

# Tooling caches. Regenerated on demand, never useful in a diff.
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local scratch output. Real results are produced on the cluster and live in
# `results/`; anything a laptop writes is a smoke test. The old top-level `res/`
# directory is gone â€” kept here so it cannot come back.
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment bookkeeping produced by the tracker pattern in scripts/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tracker.csv
results.csv
core.log
wandb/
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err
# Job logs live in the output tree (output CreditICL/<experiment>/logs/), so everything a run
# writes is in one place. The old top-level logs/ stays ignored so a stray write cannot be
# committed.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: tfm-library/ is a submodule and is tracked as a commit pointer only.
# Never add files inside it. See AGENTS.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# output CreditICL/ â€” THE single root for everything the code generates (src/utils/paths.py).
#
# Committed:  README.md (what lives where), CAPTIONS.md, All_Results.md and each notebook's
#             _figures.json â€” the readable record of a run, worth having in git history.
# Committed:  official notebook PDF figures, as requested for manuscript reuse.
# Ignored:    other PDF artifacts, job logs, run folders, benchmark scores (downloaded
#             from the cluster), checkpoints, prior pools, and any large array.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
output CreditICL/**/*.pdf
!output CreditICL/figures/**/*.pdf
output CreditICL/*/logs/
output CreditICL/*/runs/
output CreditICL/*/benchmark/
output CreditICL/*/checkpoints/
output CreditICL/*/report/
output CreditICL/*/storage_probe/
output CreditICL/prior_cache/
output CreditICL/logs/
output CreditICL/locks/
output CreditICL/adhoc/
output CreditICL/**/*.ckpt
output CreditICL/**/*.npy
output CreditICL/**/*.npz
output CreditICL/**/*.parquet
output CreditICL/**/*.pkl
output CreditICL/**/*.jsonl
output CreditICL/**/_stdout.txt

# Superseded top-level output locations, kept ignored so a stray write cannot be
# committed. LEADING SLASH matters: a bare `figures/` matches at any depth and would
# also swallow the figure folders inside output CreditICL/. `/output/` is the layout before
# 29-09-2026 (one flat tree for every experiment); `/output_CreditICL/` the name until 30-09-2026.
/output/
/output_CreditICL/
/logs/
/res/
/results/
/figures/

# Preserved September output after the root rename; never commit run artifacts.
/output CreditICL/manifests/
/output CreditICL/results/
/output CreditICL/legacy-output/
/outputCreditICL/
